A||N||10||reddog||backfire on deccel||||1||
Z||000000||reddog||11-22-2001||02:53 AM||||I was wondering if anyone knew if having the cat removed would cause backfiring on deceleration. I don't have a cat on my GT and when I decelerate or coast I get a lot of low noise popping (Sounds like popcorn popping). Is this common with exhausts that have had the cats removed? Could it be that the valves need adjusting? Should I put a resonator inline before the muffler. It's not anything terribly important and the exhaust sounds great except for deccel. Any Ideas?<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Picturenew_sig.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000001||Standard||11-22-2001||03:24 AM||||That's not backfiring, just a burble that happens 'cause of the short exhaust, I think.  My cat-less 86 v6 and 88 quad both do it.  I happen to like it.  Can't remember if my 84 duke with a cat did it or not..<P>------------------<BR>      <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sig_pic_full.jpg">          <BR><FONT COLOR="red">1988 Quad 4 Coupe 5 speed</FONT><BR><FONT SIZE="1"><FONT COLOR="white">1986 GT 5 speed, 1984 SC Auto</FONT><BR><FONT COLOR="blue">AOL: LastMinuteBastrd  AIM: SavedbyJebus</FONT></FONT>||||reg||1
Z||000002||avengador1||11-22-2001||10:35 AM||||Mine used to pop real loud before the rebuild, but now it hardly does it. It also isn't as loud when it does it now.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Avendgador1.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Fierobruiser||11-22-2001||11:34 AM||||Had a backfire popping noise when I was having coil/ignition module troubles but my 88 Duke makes the same kind of noise and resonation off and on. Louder some times than others. My mechanic seems to think that it's a loose baffle in the muffler. I guess I'll find out when I have to redo the exhaust system sometime next year. Until then I'll just always have a buzz on.<P>------------------<BR>Notchbacks Rule<BR>85GT(show car)<BR>88Coupe (daily driver)<BR>84 Coupe(project car)||||reg||1
Z||000004||cbieber||12-10-2001||10:08 PM||||I cut off my cat (got bored one day with the Sawzall) and it pops a little also on De-Acc. I have an 84 SE with the "duke". Checked timing and all of that Jazz and did not find anything out of whack. Must be the short exhaust or something in the muffler.||||reg||14
Z||000005||Jncomutt||12-10-2001||10:50 PM||||My 84 does the same thing since I got my new exhaust.  Its something to do with the hot gasses russhing out, but when your slowing down, the amount of gas coming out is also reduced, and so cold air rappidly mixes with the hot air, causing the pop.<P>Or so I was told by the muffler guy.  (If I understood him correctly)||||reg||1
Z||000006||jelly2m8||12-10-2001||11:09 PM||||Don't know for sure if removing the cat causes this, but a buddy one time put a straight pipe in there, and on decel, it left a loud pop-pop-pop.<P> We noticed he was getting black soot over the rear fascia above the exhaust tips.<P> One day while I was following him, and on decel there was a flame that shot out of each tip! WOW cool!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"><P> A few days after that he blew the muffler, we had to pry it down outa there. He did replace the cat at that point.<P> Very shortely after (like the next day) the Ignition module failed. <BR>The car didn't pop near as bad on decel after that was replaced.<P> It's possible the ign. module was gettin bad, and the cat was helping mask the pop.<P> Or it just mighta been coincedence, and was the muffler all along.<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://users.eastlink.ca/~acook1/pegged%2001.jpg">  <p>[This message has been edited by jelly2m8 (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000007||Standard||12-11-2001||02:09 AM||||generally, if an ignition module is going bad you're going to have incomplete combustion, which means the 02 sensor is going to sense a lean mixture because it detects more oxygen, so it tells the ECM to dump in more fuel to compensate.  So you get a rich mixture which tends to travel out the exhaust.  When all this hot vaporized gas gets to the end of the exhaust, it mixes with enough oxygen to spontaneously(sp?) ignite, hence the flames out the tips.  My GT does that too.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"><P>It doesn't do it with the cat on because one of the purposes of the cat is to burn any fuel vapors before they hit the atmosphere.  But too much and you just end up melting the cat.<P>For the most part, 'worn' engines (over 100,000 miles) run richer than new or freshly rebuilt ones, so they usually 'pop' more.<p>[This message has been edited by Standard (edited 12-11-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000008||84Bill||12-11-2001||11:58 AM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Standard:<BR><B> Can't remember if my 84 duke with a cat did it or not..<P></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Yep the 2.5 engines do it too, very cool sounding  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000009||Alex4mula||12-11-2001||01:30 PM||||My new catless 3.4 does it. Specially decelarating in 1st gear and a little in 2nd. I like it. It is more pronounced on higher octane gas too.<P>------------------<BR>    Alex4mula<BR>:) Red-Original Owner & White-1/94 with PM (:||||reg||1
Z||000010||fieroman_5000||12-11-2001||05:09 PM||||Does this only happen on decell?? My '84 SE 'cat-less' does this too...but also a little on accel. Any ideas?? I'm not working on it right now b/c I'm waiting till I move into my new house  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">...with a heated garage  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> <BR>Any ideas on that 'backfireing'???<P>Fieroman <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||10
